9:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose prose-lg max-w-none","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xl text-gray-700 mb-8 font-semibold","children":"Your notary bond protects the public. It does not protect you. E&O insurance is what actually covers you if a mistake turns into a lawsuit — here's what it costs and where to get it."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-3 text-sm text-gray-600 mb-8","children":[["$","img",null,{"src":"/images/ray-bearded-notary-author-photo.jpg","alt":"Ray, founder of The Bearded Notary","className":"w-10 h-10 rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-notary-gold flex-shrink-0"}],["$","p",null,{"children":["Written by"," ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/about","className":"font-semibold text-notary-navy hover:text-notary-gold hover:underline","children":"Ray"}],", former commissioned California Notary Public (2018-2022) — general notarizations and loan signings."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-gray-800 mb-8","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Disclosure:"}]," This page includes affiliate links. If you buy or sign up through them, The Bearded Notary may earn a commission at no extra cost to you."]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-notary-navy mt-12 mb-6","children":"Why a Bond Isn't Enough"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 mb-8","children":"Your state notary bond exists to protect the public, not you. If you make an error and someone files a claim, the bond issuer pays out — then comes after you to recover what they paid. One lawsuit without E&O coverage could genuinely wipe out your personal savings. E&O (errors and omissions) insurance is what protects you directly: legal defense costs, negligence claims, and claims tied to past work you've already completed."}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-notary-navy mt-12 mb-6","children":"What E&O Actually Costs"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 mb-6","children":"There are two different paths here, and they're priced differently because they're genuinely different products."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-8","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50 border-2 border-gray-200 p-6 rounded","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-notary-navy mb-3","children":"Bundled with your bond"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 mb-3","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Typical cost:"}]," $50-150/year for $25,000-$100,000 coverage"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 text-sm","children":"Many state-approved bond providers sell basic E&O alongside your notary bond at commissioning time. It's the cheapest path and covers most general notary work."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50 border-2 border-notary-gold p-6 rounded","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-notary-navy mb-3","children":"Standalone professional liability"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 mb-3","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Typical cost:"}]," Higher, priced by the carrier's own underwriting"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 text-sm","children":"A general small-business insurer, separate from your bond provider. Hiscox states its E&O coverage starts around $22.50/month, with the exact rate depending on your coverage amount, state, and risk profile."}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 mb-8","children":"Neither of these is automatically \"better\" — the bundled option is usually enough for general notarizations at lower coverage limits, while a standalone carrier can make sense if you want higher limits, broader coverage, or a provider you can deal with directly rather than through your bond issuer."}],"$Le","$Lf","$L10","$L11","$L12","$L13","$L14","$L15"]}]
